PN,30903
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FWhat is false autumn?
OL,9,FFalse autumn is an informal term used
OL,10,Fto describe a temporary spell of
OL,11,Fcooler, wetter and sometimes windier
OL,12,Fweather during late summer.
OL,14,FIt often follows a prolonged period of
OL,15,Fhot, dry conditions, making the change
OL,16,Ffeel much more dramatic than it really
OL,17,Fis.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30904
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FAfter weeks of heat, the return of
OL,8,FAtlantic weather systems can bring
OL,9,Flower temperatures, cloudier skies and
OL,10,Fmuch-needed rainfall.
OL,12,FGardens and landscapes quickly become
OL,13,Fgreener, while cooler mornings and the
OL,14,Foccasional early leaf fall can create
OL,15,Fthe impression that autumn has arrived.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30905
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FHowever, this is usually just a
OL,8,Ftemporary shift in the weather pattern
OL,9,Frather than the beginning of autumn
OL,10,Fitself. The seasons continue to
OL,11,Fprogress naturally, and there is often
OL,12,Fplenty of summer weather still to come.
OL,14,FWhy does it often happen after a very
OL,15,Fhot, dry summer?
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30906
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FExtended periods of high pressure are
OL,8,Fresponsible for many UK heatwaves,
OL,9,Fbringing prolonged sunshine and very
OL,10,Flittle rainfall. Eventually these
OL,11,Fblocking patterns weaken, allowing
OL,12,FAtlantic weather systems to return.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30907
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FAs cooler air replaces the hot
OL,8,Fcontinental air, temperatures can fall
OL,9,Fnoticeably within a day or two,
OL,10,Faccompanied by showers, stronger winds
OL,11,Fand lower daytime temperatures. After
OL,12,Fexperiencing temperatures in the high
OL,13,F20s or 30s, even values in the low 20s
OL,14,Fcan feel remarkably cool despite being
OL,15,Fclose to average for early August.
OL,17,FThis dramatic contrast is why many
OL,18,Fpeople feel that autumn has arrived,
OL,19,Feven though the meteorological summer
OL,20,Fstill has several weeks to run.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30908
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FDoes false autumn mean our heatwave
OL,8,Fsummer is over?
OL,10,FNot at all. August remains one of the
OL,11,Fwarmest months of the year in the UK,
OL,12,Fand history shows that significant
OL,13,Fheat can still develop well into
OL,14,FSeptember if the atmospheric pattern
OL,15,Fbecomes favourable.
OL,17,FA perfect example came in September
OL,18,F2023, when the UK experienced a
OL,19,Fhistoric early September heatwave.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30909
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FSome places in the UK recorded
OL,8,Ftemperatures above 30C on seven
OL,9,Fconsecutive days - the longest run of
OL,10,F30C days ever recorded in September.
OL,12,FTemperatures reached 31 to 32C across
OL,13,Fsouth-east England, while Faversham,
OL,14,FKent, recorded 33.5C on September 10,
OL,15,Fmaking it, unusually, the hottest day
OL,16,Fof the year.
OL,18,FIt was the latest point in the year to
OL,19,Fsee such a high temperature.
OL,26,@rD@COXvD@TOX
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30910
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FAlthough the most intense heat was
OL,8,Ffocused across southern England and
OL,9,FWales, temperatures also climbed into
OL,10,Fthe high 20s in Scotland and Northern
OL,11,FIreland.
OL,13,FCastlederg, County Tyrone, reached
OL,14,F28C, setting a new Northern Ireland
OL,15,FSeptember temperature record.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30911
SC,0011
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FWhile temperatures like these would
OL,8,Fnot have been unusual in July or
OL,9,FAugust, experiencing such a prolonged
OL,10,Fspell of 30C heat in September was
OL,11,Funprecedented. It demonstrated that
OL,12,Fsummer can make a dramatic return long
OL,13,Fafter many people assume autumn has
OL,14,Fbegun.
OL,16,FThe UK can also experience what is
OL,17,Ftraditionally known as an "Indian
OL,18,Fsummer".
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30912
SC,0012
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FA spell of unusually warm, settled
OL,8,Fweather during early autumn, often
OL,9,Fbringing sunshine, light winds and
OL,10,Fpleasantly warm afternoons after cool
OL,11,Fmornings.
OL,13,FWhile there is never a guarantee that
OL,14,Fsuch a pattern will develop, a cooler
OL,15,Fspell in early August certainly does
OL,16,Fnot mark the end of summer.
OL,18,FDoes a false autumn confuse wildlife?
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G12/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30913
SC,0013
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FThe effects vary between species. In
OL,8,Fmany cases, it is the prolonged hot
OL,9,Fand dry summer rather than the cooler
OL,10,Fspell itself that has the biggest
OL,11,Fimpact.
OL,13,FTrees that have experienced drought
OL,14,Fstress may begin shedding leaves weeks
OL,15,Fearlier than normal, creating an
OL,16,Fautumn-like landscape despite it still
OL,17,Fbeing summer.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G13/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30914
SC,0014
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FSome flowering plants may produce a
OL,8,Fsecond set of blooms after much-needed
OL,9,Frainfall, while birds and insects
OL,10,Foften adjust their behaviour in
OL,11,Fresponse to changing temperatures.
OL,13,FSubscribe for free to our weekly
OL,14,Fnewsletter for exclusive and original
OL,15,Fcoverage from ITV News. Direct to your
OL,16,Finbox every Friday morning.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G14/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30915
SC,0015
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FHowever, most wildlife doesn't rely on
OL,8,Ftemperature alone. Many species
OL,9,Frespond to a combination of daylight
OL,10,Flength, food availability and weather
OL,11,Fpatterns.
OL,13,FBecause daylight continues to shorten
OL,14,Fsteadily regardless of the weather, a
OL,15,Fbrief spell of cooler conditions is
OL,16,Funlikely to trigger a full seasonal
OL,17,Fchange.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G15/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30916
SC,0016
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786184293
OL,3,CWhat is false autumn? Why a cooler,
OL,4,Cwetter spell doesn't signal summer's
OL,5,Cend
OL,7,FIf warmer weather returns later in
OL,8,FAugust or September, many plants and
OL,9,Fanimals simply resume their normal
OL,10,Flate-summer behaviour.
OL,12,FSo, while false autumn may fool us
OL,13,Finto thinking the seasons have
OL,14,Fchanged, nature is often much better
OL,15,Fat recognising that summer isn't over
OL,16,Fjust yet.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G16/16
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
